From bc892456f21eee65aec5b702d02ac766df2ed9ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartheek Palla <palla.kartheekreddy@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 18:17:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(oid4vc-service): Keycloak-as-authorization-server
 issuance on v2.1.0

Ports the wallet self-service issuance capability from the fork's
oid4vc_issuer branch onto the v2.1.0 tag. That branch is 24 commits BEHIND
the release, so building from it would have dropped release fixes this
depends on - notably the SD-JWT claim reconstruction that makes DCQL
matching work. Porting forward keeps both.

Why it is needed: released v2.1.0 cannot do authenticated wallet-driven
issuance, and no configuration changes that. Issuer metadata hardcoded
itself as the authorization server, only the pre-authorised grant was
offered, and /credential accepted only self-minted tokens. All three are
now resolved:

- authorization_servers is resolved from config, so the wallet can be
  pointed at a Keycloak realm
- /credential accepts Keycloak-issued access tokens, verified against the
  realm JWKS, alongside its own pre-auth tokens
- claims are resolved at issuance from the token's subject claim to a
  registry record, through a claim-source abstraction; the caller cannot
  supply or select them

Deliberately NOT ported, to keep the change reviewable:

- tx_code/PIN verification. v2.1.0 refuses tx_code offers rather than ship
  a no-op check, and the authorization_code flow does not use it. Kept the
  release's behaviour and dropped that branch's spec.
- the demo apps, portals, registry schemas and compose files that commit
  also carried. Only services/oid4vc-service/src is ported.
- the old OFFER_REQUIRES_STAFF gate on POST /oid4vc/offer: v2.1.0's
  ENABLE_AUTH KeycloakAuthGuard supersedes it.

Taken FROM that branch where it is better: per-format credential signing
algorithm advertisement, configurable. Publishing Ed25519Signature2020 (a
Linked-Data suite) as an SD-JWT VC signing algorithm - which the release
does for every non-mdoc format - is not a value a JOSE wallet can act on.

tsc --noEmit clean; 11 suites / 127 tests pass, including the release's
own oid4vp suite.

Also includes one pre-existing local edit that was already in the working
tree: services/oid4vc-service/Makefile gains a PLATFORM flag for docker
build. Kept because the local build needs --platform linux/amd64; noted
here because it is not part of the port.
